3. Project Overview
3.1 Project Description
Demo Web Shop is a web-based e-commerce application used for demonstrating and validating online shopping workflows. The application provides customer-facing capabilities including registration, authentication, product discovery, shopping cart, wishlist, account management and ordering-related workflows.
3.2 Business Objective
The objective is to validate that core e-commerce journeys operate reliably and consistently, from customer registration and product discovery through cart management and checkout, while providing an acceptable user experience across supported browsers.
3.3 Application Overview
The publicly accessible application exposes categories such as Books, Computers, Electronics, Apparel & Shoes, Digital Downloads, Jewelry and Gift Cards, along with search, recently viewed products, product comparison, wishlist, shopping cart and account-related capabilities. The login page also provides registration, login, remember-me and forgot-password entry points.
Source: current public Demo Web Shop login page.
3.4 Testing Objective
●	Verify that business-critical customer workflows behave according to their expected behavior.
●	Identify functional defects, usability issues, validation gaps and regression defects.
●	Validate positive, negative, boundary and end-to-end scenarios.
●	Validate browser compatibility and responsive behavior for supported environments.
●	Validate critical integrations and APIs when suitable endpoints/access are available.
●	Assess performance characteristics under agreed test conditions.
●	Provide objective evidence for release readiness and stakeholder sign-off.
