22. Risk and Mitigation
Risk ID	Risk	Probability	Impact	Mitigation
R-001	Public demo environment instability or downtime	Medium	High	Schedule execution flexibly; capture environment failures; retry after stability is restored.
R-002	Application behavior changes without notice	Medium	High	Run smoke checks before suites and maintain version/date evidence.
R-003	Requirements or expected behavior unclear	Medium	High	Document assumptions and obtain stakeholder clarification before sign-off.
R-004	Test data unavailable or becomes invalid	Medium	Medium	Maintain reusable fictitious test data and data-generation approach.
R-005	Automation locator/UI changes	Medium	Medium	Use resilient locators, page objects and regular maintenance.
R-006	Third-party/dependent service unavailable	Medium	High	Identify dependency failures separately and use approved mocks/stubs where applicable.
R-007	Performance results affected by shared public infrastructure	High	High	Treat results as indicative unless a controlled performance environment is provided.
R-008	Security testing performed without authorization	Low	High	Limit testing to approved non-intrusive checks and obtain authorization for penetration testing.
R-009	Browser/device differences	Medium	Medium	Execute critical flows across agreed browser/device matrix.
R-010	Incomplete API/database access	Medium	Medium	Mark inaccessible layers as conditional scope and avoid unsupported assumptions.

